    "q-44531": {
      "dom_id": "step-q44531",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Factor $3{n}^{5}+17{n}^{4}-28{n}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Note that all of the terms have a common factor of ${n}^{3}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${n}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{n}^{5}+17{n}^{4}-28{n}^{3} & ={n}^{3}(3{n}^{2}+17n-28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the polynomial $3{n}^{2}+17n-28,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{3}(3{n}^{2}+17n-28) & = \\\\ {n}^{3}((3{n}^{2}-4n)+(21n-28)) & = \\\\ {n}^{3}((3n-4)n+(3n-4)7) & = \\\\ {n}^{3}(3n-4)(n+7)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
